{
  "analysis": "I'm in a workspace with several files including session_notes.txt, memory_plan.json, and a skill_context directory. The task requires creating a mnemonics workflow to store facts, link related ones, and provide a recall summary for project 'Northstar'. I need to first explore the workspace to understand the existing structure and any documentation.",
  "plan": "1. First, read the session_notes.txt to see what facts are available from today's discussion. 2. Read memory_plan.json to understand the expected structure. 3. Explore the skill_context directory for any documentation. 4. Then implement the mnemonics workflow based on what I find.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat session_notes.txt\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat memory_plan.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "ls -la skill_context/\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "I found session_notes.txt with facts about Project Northstar (staged rollout, concise updates, weekly status summaries, integration risk). The memory_plan.json already has some structure. I need to read the SKILL.md to understand the mnemonics workflow requirements and manifest.json for any additional context.",
  "plan": "Read the SKILL.md documentation to understand the required mnemonics workflow, then read manifest.json for additional context. This will guide how to properly store facts, link related ones, and create the recall summary.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/manifest.json\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md was truncated. I can see it's about mnemon - a persistent memory CLI for storing facts, recalling knowledge, and linking related memories. I need to see the complete documentation to understand the exact commands for remember, link, and recall operations.",
  "plan": "Read the full SKILL.md file using head/tail or less to see all the commands, then check if mnemon is installed and proceed with the workflow.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "head -200 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tail -100 skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file is being truncated. I can see the basic installation instructions but need to see the actual workflow commands (remember, link, recall) to understand how to use mnemon properly.",
  "plan": "Read the entire SKILL.md file using cat with proper handling, then check if mnemon is installed and available.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat skill_context/SKILL.md | head -400\\n",
      "duration": 0.2
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The SKILL.md file is being truncated in the output. I need to see the complete workflow section with the remember, link, and recall commands. Let me try a different approach to read the file.",
  "plan": "Use sed or awk to read specific line ranges of the SKILL.md file to see the workflow commands, and also check if mnemon is installed.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "wc -l skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "sed -n '90,150p' skill_context/SKILL.md\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "which mnemon\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Now I have the complete mnemon workflow from SKILL.md:\n- Remember: `mnemon remember \"<fact>\" --cat <cat> --imp <1-5> --entities \"e1,e2\" --source agent`\n- Link: `mnemon link <id1> <id2> --type <type> --weight <0-1> [--meta '<json>']`\n- Recall: `mnemon recall \"<query>\" --limit 10`\n\nCategories: preference, decision, insight, fact, context\nEdge types: temporal, semantic, causal, entity\n\nThe `which mnemon` returned exit code 1, so mnemon is not installed. I need to install it first.",
  "plan": "1. Check if go is available to install mnemon\n2. Install mnemon using go install\n3. Store 3 non-sensitive facts from session_notes.txt with appropriate categories:\n   - 'staged rollout' (fact)\n   - 'concise updates' (preference)\n   - 'weekly status summaries' (decision)\n4. Link related memories\n5. Recall for project 'Northstar'",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which go\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "go install github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon@latest\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Go is not available on this system. I need to try installing mnemon via Homebrew or check if there's a pre-installed binary or alternative installation method.",
  "plan": "1. Check if Homebrew is available\n2. If Homebrew is available, install mnemon via brew\n3. If not, check if mnemon is already installed somewhere or if there's a setup script",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which brew\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat setup.sh\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "brew install mnemon-dev/tap/mnemon 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Neither Go nor Homebrew is available on this system. I need to find an alternative way to install mnemon - perhaps downloading a pre-built binary or using apt/dpkg.",
  "plan": "1. Check what package managers are available (apt, curl, wget)\n2. Try to download a pre-built mnemon binary from GitHub releases\n3. If that doesn't work, check if mnemon is already installed somewhere",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which apt curl wget\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "find /usr -name 'mnemon' 2>/dev/null\\n",
      "duration": 1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest/download/mnemon-linux-amd64.tar.gz -o /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "apt is available but curl is not. I need to either install curl first or try installing mnemon directly via apt, or use wget if available.",
  "plan": "1. Check if wget is available\n2. If not, install curl via apt\n3. Then download the mnemon binary",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "which wget\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "apt-get update && apt-get install -y curl 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "curl was successfully installed via apt. Now I can download the mnemon binary from GitHub releases.",
  "plan": "1. Download the mnemon binary from GitHub releases\n2. Extract and install it\n3. Verify the installation\n4. Then proceed with the mnemonics workflow",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest/download/mnemon-linux-amd64.tar.gz -o /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 30
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The download only got 9 bytes, which suggests the URL might be incorrect or the release format has changed. Let me check what was downloaded and try alternative approaches.",
  "plan": "1. Check what was downloaded\n2. Try to find the correct release URL by checking GitHub API or trying different archive names\n3. Alternatively, check if there's a pre-built binary available elsewhere",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://api.github.com/repos/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest 2>&1 | head -100\\n",
      "duration": 10
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "The GitHub API shows the latest release is v0.1.2. I need to see the assets section to find the correct download URL for the Linux binary.",
  "plan": "1. Get the full release information including assets\n2. Download the correct binary file\n3. Install and set up mnemon",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://api.github.com/repos/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/latest 2>&1 | grep -A5 'browser_download_url'\\n",
      "duration": 10
    }
  ]
}

{
  "analysis": "Found the correct download URL for Linux amd64: https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/download/v0.1.2/mnemon_0.1.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz",
  "plan": "1. Download the correct Linux amd64 binary\n2. Extract and install it to /usr/local/bin\n3. Verify the installation\n4. Proceed with the mnemonics workflow",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "curl -L https://github.com/mnemon-dev/mnemon/releases/download/v0.1.2/mnemon_0.1.2_linux_amd64.tar.gz -o /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz 2>&1\\n",
      "duration": 30
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "tar -xzf /tmp/mnemon.tar.gz -C /tmp && ls -la /tmp/\\n",
      "duration": 1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp /tmp/mnemon /usr/local/bin/mnemon && chmod +x /usr/local/bin/mnemon\\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mnemon --version\\n",
      "duration": 1
    }
  ]
}
